    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="0671" n="1405" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1405"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mavroyeni Bey to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Legation of Turkey</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-17"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I have the pleasure to
                    give herewith copy of a telegram which I have this instant received from His
                    Excellency Tevfik Pasha, conceived in these terms: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Mr. Terrell has addressed to me two notes to express his satisfaction at
                            the conduct observed by our authorities during the late disorders, and
                            in particular renders homage to the efforts which they have put forth
                            for the protection of the life and the property of the missionaries and
                            American citizens at Harpoot, Marsovan, Aintab, and Marash.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mavroyeni.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
